1
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:04,420
- Hi.     - Hi.

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:08,920
Hi. Yeah, hi. I'm, um, Phoebe Buffay and I have babies coming out.

3
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:11,630
Okay. Have you started having contractions?

4
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:14,630
Not yet. Um, I heard they really hurt. Do they?

5
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,430
- Well...     - Oh, my God.

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,100
Which of you is the father?

7
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:23,310
None of them are. The father is my brother.

8
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:25,520
Okay.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,400
I'll miss watching you freak people out like that.

10
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:30,980
Pheebs...

11
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:33,820
This is for the babies to look at someday.

12
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:36,660
Do you want to say anything before it starts?

13
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,120
Okay. Um...

14
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:41,700
Hi, kids! Um, it's me, Aunt Phoebe.

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,120
Can't wait to see you. Please don't hurt me.

16
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:49,290
What took you so long?

17
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,710
Your cab left when ours did.

18
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:58,220
We went back because I forgot my jacket.

19
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,680
You're not wearing one.

20
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:08,060
Oh, man! I did it again!

21
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,730
Someone has to call Frank and Alice.

22
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,150
My mom might... What are you doing?

23
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,530
I've got to get the before shot.

24
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,340
We spoke to the nurse. The reason your doctor is late...

25
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,590
...is because, uh, she's not coming.

26
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,800
- What?     - She hit her head in the shower.

27
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:22,430
Oh, my God. She's so stupid!

28
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:24,760
Pheebs, it's going to be okay.

29
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:28,770
I don't see three kids coming out of your vagina.

30
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:35,400
Listen. The nurse said the doctor is wonderful.

31
00:02:35,650 --> 00:02:37,480
He's head of the department.

32
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,320
All right. Ooh. Oh, dear God, save me.

33
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,660
I'm having my first contraction.

34
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:44,950
- Oh, it's not bad.     - Okay.

35
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:50,500
And so the miracle of birth begins. And I...

36
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,920
You okay?

37
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,250
Something hurts.

38
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,340
Ooh, it's sympathy pains. Oh, that's so sweet.

39
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:00,880
I didn't know I cared that much.

40
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:04,890
- Hello.      - Hi.

41
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:08,770
I'm Dr. Harad. I'll be delivering your babies.

42
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:12,350
You'll be in good hands. I've been doing this a long time.

43
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,980
I'll be back to do your internal.

44
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:17,400
Just relax, everything looks great.

45
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:20,190
And also, I love Fonzie.

46
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:26,070
Did he just say he loves Fonzie?

47
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:28,120
That's what it sounded like.

48
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:30,000
All right.

49
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:33,370
Hey!

50
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:37,380
Am I late? Nobody came out yet, right?

51
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:40,380
No, we haven't started yet. Where's Alice?

52
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:43,970
Uh, Delaware. Until she gets here, I'll be your coach.

53
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:47,180
Don't worry. She told me about the LaMazda stuff.

54
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,640
If you get the babies out by month's end...

55
00:03:50,850 --> 00:03:52,730
...you get two percent financing.

56
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:54,440
Yeah.

57
00:03:58,020 --> 00:04:00,570
Monica, you're going to be very proud of me.

58
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:04,400
I just got us dates with two unbelievably cute nurses.

59
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:05,950
Oh, my.

60
00:04:07,370 --> 00:04:09,200
They're male nurses.

61
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:11,290
Heh, heh. Not in my head.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,670
They want to take us out Saturday night. What do you say?

63
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:18,710
Um...

64
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:23,380
- I don't think so.      - What?

65
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,090
What are you talking about?

66
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:29,050
You've been telling me to get over Ross and move on.

67
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,390
I'm moving on and so are you.

68
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,100
Why don't you want to go?

69
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:35,390
Um...

70
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,150
Why don't you give me a good reason...

71
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,690
...and I'll tell you if it's true.

72
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:45,280
- What?      - Harder than it sounds, isn't it?

73
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:48,450
You're coming. And when they get off...

74
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:51,030
...we'll go get some Jello with them.

75
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,750
Yep. There's always room for Jello.

76
00:04:58,170 --> 00:05:00,130
How do you make that dirty?

77
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:02,960
It's easy. I can do it with anything.

78
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,760
Grandma's chicken salad...

79
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,600
Ross!

80
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:18,020
Get a shot of this.

81
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:21,570
Hey, babies, these are the headlines when you were born.

82
00:05:21,770 --> 00:05:25,530
Now girl baby, turn away. And boy babies...

83
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:27,400
...check it out.

84
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:30,870
This is what naked women looked like when you were born.

85
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,660
Now let's dive into the good stuff.

86
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,660
Okay, I'm having another one.

87
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:40,750
This one doesn't hurt eith... Ooh, yes, it does! Ow.

88
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:43,050
Ow, ow, ow!

89
00:05:43,670 --> 00:05:45,380
Ooh.

90
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:48,550
Ooh, I was kind of hoping that was it.

91
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,510
Where are Monica and Rachel, anyway?

92
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:56,730
A couple of nurses asked them out. Maybe they're with them.

93
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:58,350
Really? Male nurses?

94
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:00,560
Yeah, I was bummed too.

95
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,730
So they're going on dates?

96
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,570
- When?     - I think Saturday.

97
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:10,780
- What's with him?      - Um, sympathy pains.

98
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:15,580
It was sweet at first, but now I think he's trying to steal my thunder.

99
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,040
Okay.

100
