Hey, there you are.

118
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,520
Um, there's something you should know.

119
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:24,730
Is this about you dating the nurse? Joey told me.

120
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:28,610
I am so fine. You and I, we're just, nothing.

121
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,280
Just goofing around.

122
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:37,990
Um, I was about to tell you I was getting out of it.

123
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:42,080
But, um, if we're just "goofing around," maybe I will go out with him.

124
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:44,370
Fine. Maybe I will too.

125
00:07:46,790 --> 00:07:49,460
Hey! Look what I found in the gift shop...

126
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:52,970
Oh. Get up! Get up! Get up!

127
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,180
Okay, Pheebs?

128
00:07:59,470 --> 00:08:01,100
This is Dr. Oberman.

129
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,230
He has no strong feelings about Fonzie...

130
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:07,560
...or any of the Happy Days gang.

131
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:10,650
You're going into what grade?

132
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:15,410
I'm actually a first-year resident. I graduated early.

133
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:16,780
Uh-huh. Me too.

134
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:21,580
Ross, I should have specified I'd need a grown-up doctor.

135
00:08:22,370 --> 00:08:24,040
Really, I'm fully qualified...

136
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,290
Shh, Doogie. Shh.

137
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:32,170
Doesn't anybody understand that I'm going to be having babies soon? Huh?

138
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,800
Go, little boy! Go!

139
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,010
Oh, cool. You made him cry!

140
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:50,320
Mr. Tribbiani, I'm afraid you've got kidney stones.

141
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,900
Uh, well, what else could it be?

142
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:55,110
It's kidney stones.

143
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:57,110
Or...

144
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,910
Kidney stones.

145
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:04,790
You're getting there.

146
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,250
These babies are very, very lucky.

147
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,500
They are? Why?

148
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,840
They'll be born on the Fonz's half-birthday.

149
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,970
Happy birthday.

150
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:18,470
Just to clarify.

151
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,350
I'm not Fonzie.

152
00:09:23,390 --> 00:09:24,640
Yeah.

153
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:33,480
It's a terrific thing that you're having these babies for Frank and Alice.

154
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:35,360
- I know, it is.      - Yeah.

155
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:38,070
- Can I tell you a secret?     - Yeah.

156
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,990
I want to keep one.

157
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:47,870
Oh, I'm going to be on the news.

158
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:52,880
You've gotta be kidding.

159
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:55,710
You know you can't keep one of these babies.

160
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,920
Maybe I can. You don't know.

161
00:09:58,130 --> 00:10:02,180
I do. Frank and Alice will want to keep all their children.

162
00:10:02,390 --> 00:10:04,810
Maybe not. You know?

163
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:07,350
Three babies are a handful.

164
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:09,810
Maybe they'll want to unload one.

165
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:15,570
I hate to miss an opportunity because I didn't ask.

166
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,950
Phoebe, no. This is insane.

167
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:21,280
Just ask him.

168
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:23,200
What? Me?

169
00:10:23,370 --> 00:10:24,410
I can't ask him!

170
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,950
Do you know how inappropriate that would be?

171
00:10:29,290 --> 00:10:31,790
All I'm saying is, just talk to Frank.

172
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,290
Just feel him out.

173
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:37,130
No. I will not ask Frank to give you one of his kids.

174
00:10:39,050 --> 00:10:40,090
You're right.

175
00:10:45,930 --> 00:10:47,850
Tell him it's for you.

176
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:51,810
Feeling better, sweetie?

177
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:53,810
Maybe a little.

178
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,820
Wish you hadn't seen me throw up.

179
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,610
Me too.

180
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:03,200
Hey. I just heard. What's up?

181
00:11:03,410 --> 00:11:05,280
Kidney stones.

182
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:12,540
Ordinarily, we try to break the stones up with shock waves.

183
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:15,130
But they're too close to the bladder.

184
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:19,420
Either we wait for you to pass them or else go up the urethra...

185
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:20,630
Whoa!

186
00:11:22,590 --> 00:11:25,850
No, no, no. Nothing is going "up," okay?

187
00:11:26,010 --> 00:11:30,520
"Up" is not an option. What's a urethra?

188
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:34,900
Are you crazy?

189
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:40,030
Did you ask him?

190
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,150
No, I haven't had a chance yet.

191
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,030
I'm kind of on a clock here.

192
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:48,490
Oh, Fonzie.

193
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,420
You know who I always liked? Mork.

194
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,590
Undo it. Undo it. Undo it.

195
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:03,590
Fonzie met Mork.

196
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,760
Mork froze Fonzie.

197
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,930
Yeah...

198
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:10,720
Yes...

199
00:12:11,390 --> 00:12:14,140
...but Fonzie was already cool.

200
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,230
So he wasn't hurt. Right?

201
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,690
Yeah, that's right.

202
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,200
How you doing?

203
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:27,870
Okay. Doctor says any minute now.

204
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:31,620
You know, Alice is going to be here so soon.

205
00:12:31,870 --> 00:12:36,750
You couldn't just do me a favor and, like, hold them in?

206
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:42,090
Sorry, I'm in the middle of the last favor you asked me to do.

207
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:45,720
Hey, Rachel. Hi!

208
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:49,760
This is Dan, one of the guys we're going out with on Saturday.

209
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:51,260
Dan, Monica.

210
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,600
Nice to meet you.

211
00:12:54,270 --> 00:12:55,850
Hello, Dan.

212
00:12:56,850 --> 00:13:00,820
I'm really looking forward to Saturday night. Really! Really!

213
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:05,280
So Dan...

214
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:07,490
Nurse, not a doctor, huh?

215
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,660
Kind of girlie, isn't it?

216
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:14,160
- Chandler.     - That's okay.

217
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:17,080
I'm doing this to get through medical school.

218
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,380
Oh.

219
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:22,920
And it didn't feel "girlie" during the Gulf War.

220
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,590
Sure.

221
00:13:28,510 --> 00:13:31,260
Thanks for doing that for us, by the way.

222
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,980
Why wait till Saturday? Are you free tomorrow?

223
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:39,060
Sure. I'll get somebody to cover me.

224
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:40,860
Aw, great.

225
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,020
Hey, you and me, Saturday night?

226
00:13:43,230 --> 00:13:45,240
- No.     - All right, very good!

227
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,030
This is a big one.

228
00:13:52,990 --> 00:13:55,450
Unh! Get these things out of me!

229
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:59,670
Breathe! Breathe through the pain.

230
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,880
I want the drugs, Ross!

231
00:14:05,130 --> 00:14:07,760
I do too! I do too!

232
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:13,810
Yeah, I love you. Okay, bye.

233
00:14:14,810 --> 00:14:15,890
- Hi.     - Hi.

234
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:19,020
That was Alice's mom. Alice left five hours ago.

235
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:20,560
She should be here.

236
00:14:20,770 --> 00:14:22,480
She'll make it on time.

237
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,440
- Yeah.     - Yeah.

238
00:14:24,650 --> 00:14:26,570
So Frank...

239
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:30,110
Three babies. Whoo, that just seems like a lot, huh?

240
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,160
Not to me.

241
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:35,120
Fair enough.

242
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:43,420
You're at 10 centimeters. Time to start having babies.

243
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:45,380
I want only the father here.

244
00:14:46,210 --> 00:14:48,010
- We love you.      - Good luck.

245
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,680
- Bye, Dan!     - Uh, bye, Monica.

246
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:58,020
I need a clamp, a sterile towel and Channel 31.

247
00:14:58,180 --> 00:14:59,230
What is that?

248
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:04,650
Oh, my God!

249
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:08,230
Oh, no, no! It's a good one. Fonzie plays the bongos.

250
00:15:09,650 --> 00:15:11,490
Ready? Time to try pushing.

251
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,570
Ready? Time to try peeing.

252
00:15:17,870 --> 00:15:22,080
Wait, wait, wait, wait! It's almost time to try peeing.

253
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:26,420
Push. Concentrate on pushing.

254
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:28,300
I see the head.

255
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:30,340
Yes, it is a head!

256
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:33,340
Keep pushing. Come on.

257
00:15:33,550 --> 00:15:35,890
I can't believe somebody's coming out!

258
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:38,470
There's somebody coming out of you!

259
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:40,220
It's my son!

260
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:41,850
All right.

261
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,480
Here's your first baby.

262
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,690
Yes!

263
00:15:50,030 --> 00:15:51,690
Yes! We got a baby boy!

264
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:55,530
Frank Junior, Junior!

265
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,450
How does he look?

266
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:59,040
So gross!

267
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:04,500
Okay. You ready to push again?

268
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:07,040
I already had a baby. Leave me alone.

269
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:10,590
Come on, you can do it. You can do it.

270
00:16:18,350 --> 00:16:19,760
Yeah!

271
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:23,100
Little Leslie's here! We got another one!

272
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:27,480
Oh, my God! I can't believe I have two children.

273
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,400
How scary is that?

274
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:38,570
Come on, little Chandler, it's time to be born.

275
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:41,540
He's coming! Yes, he's coming!

276
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,920
Hey, where's his thing?

277
00:16:52,130 --> 00:16:53,670
Chandler's a girl!

278
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:58,140
Oh, God. Kindergarten flashback.

279
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:03,140
They read the sonogram wrong, because they thought it was a boy.

280
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:05,440
But Chandler's a girl! Chandler's a girl!

281
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:07,310
Okay, keep saying it.

282
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:11,770
- Am I too late?     - No, no. Everything's okay.

283
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,400
There's 30 fingers and 30 toes.

284
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:16,070
We have our babies?

285
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,450
Yeah.

286
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:19,570
We have our babies.

287
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:36,090
Oh, my God.

288
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,720
You did it, man.

289
00:17:39,050 --> 00:17:40,890
Would you like to see them?

290
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,520
They're so small.

291
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,900
- I'll call you tomorrow.     - Great.

292
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:03,200
Are you really going to date that nurse man?

293
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:06,410
You and I are just "goofing around."

294
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:09,250
I thought, why not "goof around" with him?

295
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:16,340
I don't know if you've looked up "goofing around" in the dictionary.

296
00:18:16,590 --> 00:18:18,220
Well, I have...

297
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:22,180
...and the technical definition is:

298
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:26,720
"Two friends who care a lot about each other...

299
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:30,270
...and have amazing sex...

300
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:36,400
...and just want to spend more time together."

301
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:41,320
But if you have this new dictionary that gets you mad at me...

302
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:44,240
...then we have to get you my original dictionary.

303
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,790
I am so bad at this.

304
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:53,250
- You're better than you think you are.     - Really?

305
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,920
Okay. So if...

306
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:58,260
- Know when to stop.     - I sensed that I should stop.

307
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,930
- So we're okay?      - Yeah.

308
00:19:02,090 --> 00:19:04,930
I'm gonna go tell Dan that it's not going to happen.

309
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,350
- Don't do the dance.     - Right.

310
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,730
You're my favorite.

311
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:19,940
- Which one do you have?     - I don't care.

312
00:19:21,610 --> 00:19:22,660
Hi.

313
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,200
Hey.

314
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:28,080
Frank and Alice want me to tell you they're making phone calls.

315
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:31,620
Did you talk to them about, you know...

316
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:35,250
Yeah, um...

317
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,920
No, honey.

318
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,260
Oh, okay.

319
00:19:42,260 --> 00:19:44,140
It was a long shot.

320
00:19:46,930 --> 00:19:50,600
You guys? Can I just have a second alone with the babies?

321
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:52,520
Yeah.

322
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,630
So here you are.

323
00:20:16,670 --> 00:20:20,420
Seems like yesterday I was talking to you in that petri dish.

324
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:29,470
Everyone said labor was the hardest thing.

325
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,680
But they were wrong. This is.

326
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:38,150
Well, I had the most fun with you guys.

327
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:42,530
I wish I could take you home and see you every day.

328
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:48,570
I'll settle for being your favorite aunt.

329
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:54,000
I know Alice's sister has a pool, but you lived in me.

330
00:20:59,710 --> 00:21:01,500
Okay, so we're cool.

331
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,630
We're going to be great.

332
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:07,550
Little high-fives.

333
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:09,720
Aah, aah, aah.

334
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:20,270
Well, if you're going to cry...

335
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:39,790
Phoebe, we are so proud of you. You're amazing!

336
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,130
I know.

337
00:21:43,050 --> 00:21:45,170
Does it hurt as bad as they say?

338
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:47,470
You won't be able to take it.

339
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:52,680
Now that little Chandler is a girl, what'll they name her?

340
00:21:52,890 --> 00:21:54,430
They'll call her Chandler.

341
00:21:55,390 --> 00:21:58,230
Kind of a masculine name, don't you think?

342
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,900
It works on you.

